      "side": 1,
      "message": "Optional nit: I didn\u0027t realize `pkvm_cpu_initialized()` was for the given CPU, not for the current CPU... So, now this looks like a bit unneeded/unclean extra indirection: we pass `vcpu-\u003ecpu` just because we have no API returning `cpu_initialized` for the current CPU.\n\nBut I\u0027m not suggesting to add `pkvm_this_cpu_initialized()` or whatever, because actually what we are interested here is not whether _this_ CPU is already initialized but only whether the \"first\" CPU has already done the \"global\" initialization of pKVM in `initialize_global()` (so in particular, `kvm_host.xss`, uret-MSR caches etc are initialized). So, if we are thinking about this anyway, perhaps it makes sense to introduce e.g. `pkvm_global_initialized()` for that? (using WRITE_ONCE/READ_ONCE or smp_store_release/smp_load_acquire for setting/getting `global_initialized` so that it is safe?)",
      "revId": "2423d9cc84b60673567b259c44687846f031d049",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
